From ffa8a3282f867ff548d1699e5a777e13ab575651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hubert Hickman <hubert.hickman@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:15:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Expose web-only framebuffer and input to a browser host
 page

The _WEB_ONLY build already renders into an in-memory stage buffer for
Live Web. wasm_glue.cpp exports its address and geometry so the host page
can blit it to a <canvas> straight from shared wasm memory, plus a frame
counter (bumped by fbThread) so the page redraws only when something new
was staged.

Input: the page must never call functions that take HamClock mutexes from
the browser main thread (a worker holding one may be waiting on a call
proxied to that thread, which deadlocks). So the page appends events to a
lock-free single-producer queue and an input thread drains it, doing the
same as liveweb.cpp setLiveTouch()/setLiveMouse()/setLiveChar().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
